<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   RunState excludes its Room database from cloud backup and from device-to-device
   transfer, for the reasons recorded in backup_rules.xml.

   The two channels are listed separately and deliberately. They are independent: a
   rule under cloud-backup says nothing about device-transfer, so an exclusion that
   appeared in only one of them would still hand the database to the other. Both are
   withheld, because a directly transferred run is exactly as unreconcilable as a
   restored one while no synchronization or restore handling exists.

   The whole database domain is excluded rather than just runstate.db, so the -wal and
   -shm sidecar files cannot travel independently of the database they belong to.

   allowBackup stays true, and this exclusion is temporary.

   This file is what Android 12 (API 31) and higher read; Android 11 (API 30) and lower
   read backup_rules.xml.
   See https://developer.android.com/about/versions/12/backup-restore#xml-changes
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>